{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 (Direction C.c1) — implemented and proven locally, but STOPPED at the review-plan exit gate on a SUBSTANTIVE design objection (G6). Escalating to the operator; no --force, worktree retained.\n\n### What is done (worktree ../debug-1c0d-indeterminate, staged, NOT committed/pushed)\n\nThe operator-approved C.c1 fix is fully implemented and validated locally, entirely with mocked/injected providers (NO real Bedrock load):\n\n- **Fix**: `should_fall_back` now returns True only for `RETRY_NOW` or `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` (drops `WAIT_AND_RETRY` and the `_RETRYABLE` coupling). `failure._RETRYABLE` unchanged — a throttle stays exit-11 retryable, it just no longer fails over.\n- **RED→GREEN**: held-out oracle `tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` failed for the right reason pre-fix (throttle→True) and passes post-fix; byte-identical to its pre-fix snapshot (not weakened).\n- **End-to-end replication** (Exp-C, real `FallbackModel` + real `should_fall_back`): a `ModelHTTPError(429)` throttle primary + keyless-`TypeError` fallback — post-fix the fallback is NEVER reached (`calls==['primary']`) and the throttle surfaces as `WAIT_AND_RETRY`/`retryable=True` (exit-11), NOT INDETERMINATE.\n- **Mutation check with teeth** (inside `sandbox-exec`, host has no `timeout`): re-introducing `WAIT_AND_RETRY` into the failover set makes BOTH the oracle and the replication go RED — the replication reproduces the exact incident signature (`TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method…`). Restored → GREEN.\n- 200 related tests pass; `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean. Out-of-artifact consumer (`test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py` 503 case) + stale docs (`rebar.toml`, `docs/local-dev-env.md`) updated to the new contract.\n\n### The exit gate blocked THREE times; the first two were plan-hygiene, the third is a DESIGN objection\n\n1. **P1/P10 (deterministic floor, no LLM)** — needed an exact `## Acceptance Criteria` `- [ ]` checklist + a `## Testing` section. Fixed.\n2. **G1G2** — the plan's Scope omitted an out-of-artifact consumer (`test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py`, the 503 case). Enumerated all six touched files. Fixed.\n3. **G6 (critical, LLM tier) — the core-scope objection, verified CORRECT:** excluding the ENTIRE `WAIT_AND_RETRY` class disables cross-provider failover for a genuine primary OVERLOAD/timeout, not just a plain 429 throttle.\n\n### G6 is factually right (verified empirically against `classify_llm_failure`)\n\n`WAIT_AND_RETRY` ⊋ \"plain Bedrock 429\". It also covers `529`, `503`, `500/502/504`, `httpx.ReadTimeout`, and botocore read/connect timeouts. `RETRY_NOW` covers ONLY `httpx.ConnectError`/`ConnectTimeout` and a bare `ModelAPIError`. So broad C.c1 also stops a genuine Bedrock **overload/timeout** (surfaced as `ModelHTTPError(5xx)`) from failing over — and with a PRESENT `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (e.g. CI), that failover is the legitimate availability rescue 8fbd was designed and operator-approved for. (Note: in the pure Anthropic path a 5xx surfaces as a bare `ModelAPIError`→`RETRY_NOW` and still fails over; the loss bites the Bedrock-PRIMARY frontier chain, which is exactly review-plan's default.)\n\n### The decision (operator's call) — three directions\n\n- **A. Keep broad C.c1 as authorized** (exclude the whole `WAIT_AND_RETRY` class). Consistent with \"restore pre-8fbd\" (pre-8fbd frontier had NO fallback, so nothing failed over). Simplest; most robust against the keyless-fallback trap across ALL transient classes. COST: a genuine Bedrock overload/timeout no longer fails over even when a key is present. To clear G6 the plan must explicitly OWN that tradeoff (operator accepts it) and ideally scope the credential-guard (C) as follow-up. This is an operator design acceptance, which is why I'm not asserting it unilaterally.\n- **B. Narrow to the plain rate-limit 429 only** — keep 529/503/5xx/timeout failover-eligible. Preserves overload-rescue. COST: needs to distinguish throttle-from-overload inside the taxonomy (split `WAIT_AND_RETRY` into THROTTLE vs OVERLOAD, or re-introduce a status-code check in `should_fall_back` — the exception-type coupling cc33 deliberately removed). Also still fails a genuine 5xx overload over to a KEYLESS fallback, so it does not fully close the \"keyless masks a transient\" class for 5xx.\n- **C. Root-guard: refuse failover to a credential-UNREACHABLE fallback** — keep `WAIT_AND_RETRY` failover-eligible, but don't fail over to a fallback whose key is absent (the actual defect: the frontier fell over to a KEYLESS `anthropic:opus`). Directly matches this bug's attribution (\"8fbd enabled failover without a credential-reachable-fallback guard\") and preserves overload-rescue when a key IS present. COST: needs credential-presence detection at the fallback boundary; larger change than a one-line predicate edit.\n\n**Recommendation:** C is the truest root-cause fix (it fixes the \"keyless fallback masks a transient\" defect for the WHOLE transient class while preserving legitimate rescue); A is the acceptable minimal choice IF the operator explicitly accepts losing Bedrock-overload failover and books C as follow-up; B is least attractive (partial + taxonomy churn). Per the debug protocol I STOPPED at the gate, did not `--force`, and retained the worktree pending the operator's direction."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788049771154402359,"uuid":"eb02042b-a3a5-493d-aadc-15bc29ff122a"}